  {
   "id": "concept1",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Short-run cost concepts"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "In the short run, total fixed cost (TFC) does not change with output (rent, interest, permanent staff) and total variable cost (TVC) rises with output (raw materials, wages of casual labour). $TC = TFC + TVC$. Per-unit costs: $AFC = TFC/q$, $AVC = TVC/q$, $AC = TC/q = AFC + AVC$. Short-run marginal cost is the change in total cost from one more unit: $SMC = \\Delta TC/\\Delta q = \\Delta TVC/\\Delta q$."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "TC = TFC + TVC"
    },
    {
     "en": "AC = AFC + AVC"
    },
    {
     "en": "SMC = ΔTC/Δq = ΔTVC/Δq"
    },
    {
     "en": "At q = 0, TC = TFC"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "Total cost is fixed cost plus variable cost. Dividing by output gives average costs, and marginal cost is the extra cost of one more unit.",
    "kn": "ಒಟ್ಟು ವೆಚ್ಚ = ಸ್ಥಿರ ವೆಚ್ಚ + ಬದಲಾಗುವ ವೆಚ್ಚ. ಉತ್ಪನ್ನದಿಂದ ಭಾಗಿಸಿದರೆ ಸರಾಸರಿ ವೆಚ್ಚಗಳು; ಇನ್ನೊಂದು ಘಟಕದ ಹೆಚ್ಚುವರಿ ವೆಚ್ಚ ಸೀಮಾಂತ ವೆಚ್ಚ."
   },
   "formula": "AC = AFC + AVC,\\quad SMC = \\frac{\\Delta TC}{\\Delta q}"
  },
