  {
   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Shapes of short-run cost curves"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "TFC is a horizontal line; TVC starts from the origin; TC starts from the TFC level and runs parallel to TVC. AFC is a rectangular hyperbola that falls throughout. AVC, AC and SMC are U-shaped because of the law of variable proportions: as MP of the variable input rises, cost per unit falls, and as MP falls, cost per unit rises. SMC cuts AVC and AC at their minimum points. The gap between AC and AVC (= AFC) narrows as output rises, and minimum AC lies to the right of minimum AVC."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "AFC: rectangular hyperbola"
    },
    {
     "en": "AVC, AC, SMC: U-shaped (law of variable proportions)"
    },
    {
     "en": "SMC cuts AVC and AC at their minima"
    },
    {
     "en": "Min AC is to the right of min AVC"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "AFC keeps falling. AVC, AC and marginal cost are U-shaped, and marginal cost cuts AVC and AC at their lowest points.",
    "kn": "ಸರಾಸರಿ ಸ್ಥಿರ ವೆಚ್ಚ ನಿರಂತರವಾಗಿ ಇಳಿಯುತ್ತದೆ. ಸರಾಸರಿ ಬದಲಾಗುವ ವೆಚ್ಚ, ಸರಾಸರಿ ವೆಚ್ಚ ಮತ್ತು ಸೀಮಾಂತ ವೆಚ್ಚ U ಆಕಾರದಲ್ಲಿವೆ; ಸೀಮಾಂತ ವೆಚ್ಚ ಅವುಗಳ ಕನಿಷ್ಠ ಬಿಂದುಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ಛೇದಿಸುತ್ತದೆ."
   }
  },
